# The public hosts a review comment or a pull request may name. One per line: the
# host, then why it is here. An entry allows the host and every name under it. This
# is the format of scripts/private_scan.allow in those-who-run/paddock, whose rules
# this package ports; a job adds its own entries with an allow file at run time.

# Code, images and packages.
github.com                The organisation's code host, and noreply commit addresses.
raw.githubusercontent.com GitHub's raw files.
ghcr.io                   GitHub's container registry, where the org's images are published.
docker.io                 Docker Hub, where pinned base images come from.
golang.org                Go's module paths (golang.org/x/...).
go.dev                    Go's documentation and package index (pkg.go.dev).
pypi.org                  The Python package index.
npmjs.com                 The npm registry.
buf.build                 Buf's registry and documentation.
anthropic.com             The noreply address in the Co-Authored-By trailer of agent commits.
claude.com                Claude Code's site, linked in the line Claude Code adds to a PR body.

# Kubernetes and Argo CD API groups and label prefixes, which are names, not hosts.
k8s.io                    Kubernetes API groups (batch.k8s.io, networking.k8s.io).
kubernetes.io             Kubernetes' well-known labels and its documentation.
argoproj.io               Argo CD's annotations.

# Documentation and specifications a review cites.
docs.nats.io              NATS's documentation.
www.conventionalcommits.org The Conventional Commits specification.
protobuf.dev              Protocol Buffers' documentation.
connectrpc.com            Connect's documentation.
duckdb.org                DuckDB's documentation.
